1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,268
And here on Radio Rivenden we have Lynne Rawley, the Public Relations Officer of

2
00:00:06,268 --> 00:00:08,317
our own Rivenden City Theatre.

3
00:00:08,317 --> 00:00:09,100
Hello, Lynne.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:09,760
Hello.

5
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:14,800
Now, the theatre is reopening soon after its three-year redevelopment programme, isn't it?

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,400
That's right,

7
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,500
and there are a lot of improvements.

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,578
The first thing people will see when they go in is that the foyer

9
00:00:21,578 --> 00:00:24,200
has been repainted in the original green and gold.

10
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,334
Then the box office has been reoriented.

11
00:00:26,334 --> 00:00:30,602
with its own access from the side of the building instead of through the

12
00:00:30,602 --> 00:00:30,907
foyer,

13
00:00:30,907 --> 00:00:33,346
which means it can be open longer hours,

14
00:00:33,346 --> 00:00:34,870
and has more space, too.

15
00:00:34,870 --> 00:00:37,689
The shop that used to be in the foyer,

16
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:42,074
which sold books and CDs, is the one part of the redevelopment which isn't

17
00:00:42,074 --> 00:00:42,700
yet complete.

18
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:46,805
The plan is to find new premises for it near the theatre,

19
00:00:46,805 --> 00:00:49,200
and we've had difficulty finding somewhere suitable.

20
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,150
We hope to reopen the shop in the next few months.

21
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:56,130
Will audiences find any difference in the auditorium?

22
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:59,880
Yes, we've increased the leg-room between the rows.

23
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,185
This means that there are now fewer seats but we're sure audiences will be

24
00:01:04,185 --> 00:01:04,800
much happier.

25
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,342
And we've installed air conditioning,

26
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:08,810
so it won't get so hot and stuffy.

27
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:12,165
We already had a few seats which were suitable for wheelchair users,

28
00:01:12,165 --> 00:01:14,122
and now there are twice as many,

29
00:01:14,122 --> 00:01:15,800
which we hope will meet demand.

30
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,850
Something else that will benefit audiences is the new lifts.

31
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:22,800
The two we used to have were very small and slow.

32
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,890
They've now gone and we've got much more efficient ones.

33
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:28,060
Anything for the performers?

34
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:31,330
Yes, we've made a number of improvements backstage.

35
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:36,035
The small dark dressing rooms we used to have have been converted into two

36
00:01:36,035 --> 00:01:37,043
large airy rooms,

37
00:01:37,043 --> 00:01:39,060
so they're much more comfortable now.

38
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:43,900
And the state- of-the-art electronic sound and lighting systems have been installed.

39
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:44,384
OK,

40
00:01:44,384 --> 00:01:50,680
so what's the first play that audiences can see when the theatre reopens?

41
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:54,894
We've got a very exciting production of Peter Shaffer's Royal Hunt of the Sun,

42
00:01:54,894 --> 00:01:56,700
which is currently touring the country.

43
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:00,510
That starts on October the 13th and runs till the 19th.

44
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:03,840
We're experimenting a bit with the time the curtain goes up.

45
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:07,094
We used to start all our performances at 7.30,

46
00:02:07,094 --> 00:02:11,323
but that made it difficult for people to go home by public transport,

47
00:02:11,323 --> 00:02:13,276
so instead we're beginning at 7,

48
00:02:13,276 --> 00:02:14,577
because at 9.45,

49
00:02:14,577 --> 00:02:17,180
when it finishes, there are still buses running.

50
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:18,890
Tickets are already selling fast.

51
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:25,386
The Friday and Saturday performances sold out almost immediately and, in fact, now there are only tickets for Monday

52
00:02:25,386 --> 00:02:26,070
and Thursday.

53
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:27,460
How much are they?

54
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:30,260
We've introduced a simpler price structure.

55
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:36,720
Ticket prices used to range from ￡6 to ￡30 but now they're all ￡18.

56
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:42,102
They're available from the box office, in person, by phone, fax or post,

57
00:02:42,102 --> 00:02:42,930
or online.

58
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:46,000
OK, Lynne, now if you'd like to give the contact details for the theatre...
